name: Draft, explicitly review and selectively reuse a lesson in immutable context
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py prepare @TMP_TARGET @ART
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 F-0001 · FINDING | original-observation
submit: lessons
require-live-snap: 25 REUSABLE LESSONS | empty-lessons
keys: n
require-live-snap: 20 LESSON DRAFT | title-field
paste-file: @ART/title.txt
keys: Tab
paste-file: @ART/text.txt
require-live-snap: 20 Unicode café | multiline-field
ask: Does the lesson field own the multiline Unicode paste, preserve the composer, and show the four-field flow and human-review boundary?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: editor-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: editor-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: editor-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: editor-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: editor-40x12
ask: Is the active field readable at each size with its cursor and clear edit, review and back controls?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 REUSABLE LESSONS | retained-browser
keys: d
require-live-snap: 20 Unicode café | resumed-draft
keys: Tab
paste-file: @ART/applies.txt
keys: Tab
paste-file: @ART/limits.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM LESSON DRAFT | draft-confirmation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py draft-confirmation @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does confirmation expose the complete lesson, applicability, limitations and original finding before any write?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Draft · Greeting | saved-draft
resize: 40x12
live-snap: draft-browser-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: draft-detail-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py draft @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: a
paste-file: @ART/reason.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM ACCEPTED LESSON | accept-confirmation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py accept-confirmation @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does accepting a lesson require a reason and a second explicit Enter, show the original generation and source snapshot, and leave future scans separate?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Accepted · Greeting | accepted-lesson
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py accepted @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: n Tab
paste-file: @ART/retained.txt
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this unsubmitted note | retained-before-copy
keys: Escape
keys: Space u
require-live-snap: 25 LESSONS INTO CONTEXT | base-picker
expect: Selected lessons: 1.
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Enter creates copy | copy-confirmation
expect: Base: Owned lesson context
expect: Greeting review lesson · revision 2
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py copy-confirmation @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does copy confirmation name the selected base and lesson revisions, retain their exact references, and explain that the active context and finding decisions remain unchanged?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: copy-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: copy-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: copy-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: copy-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
require-live-snap: 20 Base: Owned lesson | copy-base-40x12
expect: Greeting review lesson
expect: Enter copy
expect: Esc base
expect: Home/End read
keys: PageDown
require-live-snap: 20 active context | copy-meaning-40x12
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 sha256: | copy-references-40x12
keys: PageUp
live-snap: copy-pageup-40x12
keys: Home
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Choose the exact base | restored-base-picker
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Greeting review lesson | restored-copy-confirmation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py copy-confirmation @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Can the named choices and full references be read across all six sizes, with bounded Home/End paging and an unchanged selection after returning to the base picker, without creating the copy early?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Saved context: | saved-copy
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py copy @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: d
require-live-snap: 20 Keep this unsubmitted note | retained-after-copy
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py retained-copy @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Can the unsubmitted multiline draft be resumed after copying accepted lessons, without saving that draft or changing its text and selected field?
keys: Escape
keys: t
paste-file: @ART/retire.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM RETIRED LESSON | retire-confirmation
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Retired · Greeting | retired-lesson
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py retired @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: lessons
require-live-snap: 25 Retired · Greeting | recovered-lessons
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/reviewed_lessons.py restart @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does no-color restart retain the lesson, origin and retirement with no new model work, while the immutable copy remains inspectable and unusable for scans?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
